Z||000000||88/2.8||11-09-2000||10:35 AM||||Anyone know what the biggest size tire is that can fit in there and look good w/ stock 15'' rims?||||reg||6
Z||000001||Oreif||11-09-2000||10:40 AM||||Since I assume yours is an 88 by your screen name, The front wheels are 6" wide and the rears are 7" wide. You can go to 225 on the rear and 215 on the front. Max is 235 in back and 225 in front but not recommended for hard cornering.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88/2.8||11-09-2000||11:02 AM||||ok, thanks but can you also reccommend a good brand of tire?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-09-2000||11:06 AM||||I prefer BFGoodrich. There are many good tires to choose from. My 86 SE is lowered and I have 87 GT wheels on it (15X7) so I am running 225/50R15's all the way around.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88/2.8||11-09-2000||11:08 AM||||Wow! I'd like to see a picture of that.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Oreif||11-09-2000||11:10 AM||||Ask and Ye shall receive!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/All_pics.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000006||ThatRickGuy||11-09-2000||11:20 AM||||I've got 225s on all 4 wheels, their a little old and beat up, but I have still not gotten the front end to push at all. only problem is parking... trying to turn the stearing wheel w/ those big chunks of rubber is about hard as heck!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||11-09-2000||11:42 AM||||I was running 215's at all four corners, but went back to 205's on the front.  I felt the steering was getting a little too stiff with the wider tires on the front.  Thats just a personal preference of course... IMO its just more fun with the smaller tires up there.<P>I have Dunlop D60 A2's and love them.  They have great dry and wet weather traction, and are wearing well.  I have heard a lot of people who also like the BFGoodrich tires as Orief mentioned too!  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||11-09-2000||07:02 PM||||Hey Orief, did you happen to drive through Michigan earlier this week? I saw a car like yours and was wondering.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||11-09-2000||07:17 PM||||It couldn't have been mine. Mine is in the garage with 1/2 the interior ripped out. Working on the stereo system. It's been in the garage for 3 weeks now. It's probably someone who has seen my car and copied it! That means I'll have to change it again. Maybe paint it flash yellow or pearlized white with a candy blue and gold dust clearcoat!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">   <P>Nah I like it black!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||88formula||11-09-2000||09:15 PM||||Did you guy’s know that bigger tires hurts your acceleration and gas mileage. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Bob Englert||11-09-2000||09:38 PM||||I can understand the effect on acceleration since it does have a little bit of an effect on the overall gearing, but it should only help mileage.  Larger diameter tires will travel farther per revolution.  You won't actually see any apparent mileage difference unless you also get the speedometer recalibrated.  It will just appear that you have travel less distance than you did before.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>87 Coupe<BR>85 SE (For Sale)||||reg||1
Z||000012||Vlad||11-10-2000||01:53 AM||||That was also my question. <BR>I have 235/60 R14 in all coners that I got with a car from prevous owner and I hate them. The brand is Cheetah something. This seems to be division of Cooper.<BR>They are not good in wet breaking.<P>Also, I blame them for my bad gas mileage (15 mph). It has to be very hard to turm them for engine. <BR>BTW, what else can be the reason for such a gas results. No codes,EGR fine, calipers and pads not draging, cat.converter seems to be OK, no hard driving. <BR>Car drives fine, stady idling 800-900 when hot, 1500 when cold. The pipes smell rich though... Leaking engectors...?? <BR>Anything else?<P>85 V6||||reg||1
Z||000013||Oreif||11-10-2000||09:11 AM||||88Formula, That is the reason I went with the 225/50R15's. The stock size tire for my SE was a 215/60R14. The tires I have now are very close to the same diameter as the original's but wider. This has minimal affect on speedo and mileage.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tom88gt||11-10-2000||10:18 AM||||OK, I'll jump in too.  <P>My vote is for the Dunlop D60 A2 as well.  A Consumer Reports best buy in the performance touring category, I think.  Cheap too.  Put them on my 300ZX Turbo, Volvo 740T, Porsche 914, put some Dunlop Radial Rovers on my Jeep.  I think a great tire brand/value.  I want great dry weather handling but I want to be safe in the rain too (I've lost control in the rain on pure performance tires and it scared the $hit outta me).||||reg||14
